2. SUPABASE - LIVE DATA LEAK CLOSED AND VERIFIED:
   - Applied supabase/migrations/20260822090000_security_and_performance_hardening.sql
     directly to the live project via MCP (approved by user after disclosure):
     * CRITICAL: profiles table had a public-role SELECT policy (qual=true)
       exposing every user's subscription_tier/search_count/full_name to
       anyone with the anon key, unauthenticated. Restricted to
       auth.uid() = id.
     * RLS initplan fix on profiles insert/update policies.
     * Dropped a duplicate SELECT policy on grants.
     * Revoked RPC-callable EXECUTE on handle_new_user()/rls_auto_enable()
       (had to REVOKE FROM PUBLIC, not just anon/authenticated -- Postgres
       grants EXECUTE to PUBLIC by default).
     * Pinned search_path on 2 functions, dropped 2 duplicate indexes,
       added missing FK index on action_plans.match_id.
   - LIVE VERIFICATION: ran an actual signup against
     https://p-search-mobil.vercel.app, confirmed via SQL that auth.users
     insert -> handle_new_user trigger -> profiles row creation all still
     work correctly under the new RLS/grant rules. Test account deleted
     after verification.
   - Left open (risk/benefit): vector extension still in public schema
     (moving it risks breaking the just-built embeddings feature); Leaked
     Password Protection is Supabase Pro-plan-only (user's call).
   - Technical debt noted, not fixed: profiles->auth.users,
     business_profiles->profiles, grant_matches->business_profiles FKs are
     ON DELETE NO ACTION, not CASCADE -- account deletion would fail today.
     Not urgent: no account-deletion feature exists yet in the app.

